# Documentation maintenance

Before finishing any feature, fix, or refactor, run the **Documentation Maintenance Loop** in `AGENTS.md` (loop 6).

Unless the change is trivial (typo, comment-only):

1. Update `AGENTS.md` — repository map, design system, eval table, agent loops, env/commands as triggered.
2. Update `README.md` — features, migrations, project layout, testing list, scripts as triggered.
3. In handoff, list doc files updated or say explicitly why none were needed.

For `lib/` eval work, also follow `.cursor/rules/eval-modules.mdc`.

Run `npm run check:docs` when eval tests or doc lists change — CI runs the same check.

Do not defer doc updates to a follow-up unless the user explicitly asks to skip them.
